From cfa14a9f11a5c08588706856a16d227f4fe54cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:55:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: restore MT6897 C-PHY MMSYS routing on power-on

Restore the documented no-swap C-PHY lane fields on each first link power-on, holding explicit parent MMSYS PM and configuration-clock references until final link teardown. Each dual-link half uses its own parent bank. Preserve reserved fields and leave other SoCs and D-PHY routing unchanged.

Adapt the register sequence from the pinned vendor implementation, rather than importing its broader PHY policy. Known-good MT6897 routing is LSB=0 and MSB=0x62101. The missing restore is a source-supported resume hypothesis; it has not yet passed a physical power-cycle trial.

Balance format/PHY/acquisition failures, track successful bridge and DDP owners, and reject host commands until both the addressed link and lead have completed initialization. Portable tests exercise the actual power, callback, transfer and register-helper functions with dual-link failures and simulated context loss.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_mipi_tx.c
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
